      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:7:32:1",
      "text": [
        " كَتَبْتُ إِلَيْهِ يَعْنِي أَبَا الْحَسَنِ الْأَوَّلَ ( عليه السلام ) أَسْأَلُهُ عَنِ السِّكَنْجَبِينِ وَ الْجُلَّابِ وَ رُبِّ التُّوتِ وَ رُبِّ التُّفَّاحِ وَ رُبِّ السَّفَرْجَلِ وَ رُبِّ الرُّمَّانِ فَكَتَبَ حَلَالٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "A number of our companions, from Sahl Bin Ziyad, form Mansour Bin Al Abbas, from Ja’far Bin Ahad Al Makfouf who said, ",
          "‘I wrote to him<sup>asws</sup>, meaning Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> the 1st asking him<sup>asws</sup> about the ginger drink, and the rose water, and the mulberry jam, and the apple jam, and the quince jam, and the pomegranate jam. So he<sup>asws</sup> wrote: ‘Permissible’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "1. A number of our people have narrated from Sahl ibn Ziyad from Mansur ibn al-‘Abbas from Ja‘far ibn Ahmad al-Makfuf who has said the following: “I once wrote to him, meaning, abu al-Hassan, al-Awwal, ‘Alayhim al-Salam, and asked about oxymel, rose water, jam of mulberry, apple, quince and pomegranate. He (the Imam) said in writing, ’It is lawful. 5 ” "
        ]
      }
